\f1\fs22 Chanta cheered up, in part because Solo has promised he\'92d see Sarah again (in Dubai, wherever the tax that was). There was also the frequency and number of groupies he was fucking.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta woke to the sound of birds singing from ruined rooftops and entangled power lines. His first thought, as he blinked his eyelashes unglued: the ceiling was the cleanest he\'92d ever slept under. In one outstretched hand, he still held a bottle of Livid Emu whiskey; the other was pinned under Betty Lee, one of the growing number of Elvisettes who made sure his every whim was catered for, except for every time he whimsically ordered to leave him the tax alone.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta was beginning to understand how suffocated Sarah must have felt in the mansion. If the Elvi attributed saintliness to the Holy Momma, they were ascribing the base bacchanalian appetites of a devil to him. The men loved drinking with him, and women loved\'85 well they loved very well, thank you very much. Which mostly suited Chanta just fine, if only he had a single moment\'92s peace to himself once in a while.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta delicately tried to extract his arm out from under Betty Lee. She moaned and rolled away, which gave him opportunity to slide free. He hunched up on his elbow, drained the dregs of whiskey, and let the bottle slide to the floor behind.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As his eyes toured like a slow-moving Cadillac around the curves and corners of Betty Lee\'92s naked body\'97and the bodies of Marguerita and Princess Shalimar snuggled behind her\'97Chanta marvelled at how they appeared more beautiful with each passing day. As he traced his finger over the smooth satin skin of Betty Lee\'92s hip, he thought, 
\f2\i Is this love?
\f1\i0  and admitted to himself he wouldn\'92t have a clue. He\'92d never been in love before, unless he counted the forlorn infatuations for Airborne girls he\'92d indulged in since he was a boy. If not love, then why was he no longer noticing their imperfections? He could no longer see the crow\'92s feet by Betty Lee\'92s eyes, the first signs of grey in her hair, the little roll of fat he was sure she\'92d had the first time he saw her unclothed. Marguerita and Princess Shalimar looked equally flawless. What was this?\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As if scalded, he sharply withdrew his hand away from Betty Lee; he\'92d been tracing Sarah\'92s name repeatedly on her butt.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta rose and, on his way to the bathroom, almost tripped over a naked Elvisette sleeping on the floor at the foot of the bed. His tip-toeing around her failed when another infatuated fan leaped out of the closet and hollered, \'93Surprise.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta jumped with fright, and the sleeping Elvisette roused. Betty Lee woke quickly, vaulted over Marguerita and Princess Shalimar, squared up to the invader. With a military snap she pointed at the door and ordered, \'93Out!\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The invader\'92s shoulders slumped. \'93Can I just get an autograph?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chanta smiled, Betty Lee relented. The invader pulled a marking pen from her jeans pocket, offered it to Chanta, and unbuttoned her blouse. Chanta signed over her collar bone while Betty Lee looked on like an unimpressed overseer, and the other three snuggled on the bed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Singing could be heard from the balcony. A half dozen Elvisettes huddled close to the glass doors, singing 
\f2\i Evolve Me Tender
\f1\i0 .\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93How\'92d they get up here?\'94 Betty Lee asked, disbelieving.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>One of the singers held up a grappling hook and a heavy rope. Chanta was amused; they\'92d got some of the lyrics wrong, but substituting \'93love\'94 for \'93evolve\'94 was possibly an improvement. He threw open the doors.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You\'92re not letting them in,\'94 Betty Lee shrieked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Nah,\'94 Chanta answered. \'93But they deserve autographs too.\'94 He twiddled the marker still in his hand and retrieved a note pad. The Elvisettes outside stopped singing and squealed with joy as Chanta scribbled and handed out pages.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>One of the singers beheld her new trophy with adoration which quickly turned to confusion and scorn. \'93Who is Tony Chantara? We want the Great Teacher.\'94\
