\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>After showering, Chanta relented and dressed in the jumpsuit that had been specially designed and crafted for the Great Teacher.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93There\'92s too much gold in it,\'94 he complained to Princess Shalimar as he zipped up. His complaint was about both the colour and the material. Real gold thread was woven into the fabric, and it reflected light in unpredictable, vision-impairing ways. Chanta almost blinded himself when he turned the light on during his last bathroom visit, and only survived by grabbing a pair of sunglasses someone had left by the sink and shoving them firmly on the bridge of his nose.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He refused to wear the poncho.
